---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../site.config";
---

<Base title="Terms of use" description={`Terms of use for the ${siteConfig.name} website.`}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <p
      class="rounded-card border-accent/30 bg-accent/10 text-ink border px-4 py-3 text-sm"
      role="note"
    >
      This page is a starting point, not legal advice. Have a lawyer licensed in
      {siteConfig.jurisdiction}
      review it before you publish it.
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display mt-8 text-4xl tracking-tight">Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="text-muted mt-3">Last updated: {"{{effective date}}"}</p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-[17px] leading-7">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">Agreement</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          These terms govern your use of the website operated by
          {siteConfig.legalName}
          (“{siteConfig.name}”, “we”, “us”) at this domain. By using the site, you agree to these
          terms. If you do not agree, do not use the site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">The site</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The site is provided for general information about {siteConfig.name}. Content may change
          without notice and may not always be complete or up to date.
          {"{{describe the services or goods offered}}"}. Nothing on the site is professional advice
          unless we have a separate written agreement with you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">Acceptable use</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You may not use the site in a way that is unlawful, that interferes with other people or
          with our systems, or that tries to probe, scrape, or overload the site. You are
          responsible for the accuracy of information you send us through the contact form or by
          email.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">Intellectual property</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The text, design, logos, and other content on this site are owned by
          {siteConfig.legalName}
          or used under licence. You may not copy or reuse them for commercial purposes without our
          written permission, except for the limited personal use that the law already allows.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The site is provided “as is.” To the fullest extent permitted by the laws of
          {siteConfig.jurisdiction}, we are not liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential
          damages arising from your use of the site. {"{{liability cap, if any}}"}. This does not
          exclude liability that the law does not allow us to exclude.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">Governing law</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          These terms are governed by the laws of {siteConfig.jurisdiction}, without regard to
          conflict-of-law rules. The courts of {siteConfig.jurisdiction} have exclusive jurisdiction
          over disputes arising from these terms or the site, unless a law that applies to you says
          otherwise.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">Changes and contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We may update these terms from time to time. The “Last updated” date will change when we
          do. Questions about these terms can be sent to
          <a
            class="decoration-line underline underline-offset-4"
            href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}
            >{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
